.TH ABL-EXORCIST-ASSEMBLER 1 "September 2026" "abl-exorcist-assembler 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
abl-exorcist-assembler \- construct mainline kernel payloads for abl-exorcist
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B abl-exorcist-assembler
.I KERNEL SHIM
> \fIOUTPUT\fR
.br
.B abl-exorcist-assembler --ramdisk
.I KERNEL INITRD
> \fIOUTPUT\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B abl-exorcist-assembler
is the host-side tool for constructing payloads consumed by the
.B abl-exorcist
AArch64 shim.
It accepts a raw arm64 Image, a gzip- or zstd-compressed Image, or a Linux EFI
zboot image and converts it to a validated raw arm64 Image before assembly.
.PP
The default mode appends a compressed kernel package to a raw
device-appropriate shim.
The
.B --ramdisk
mode emits an ABLXRD1 container holding the compressed kernel followed by the
supplied initrd bytes.
Both modes write the assembled binary to standard output.
.PP
Device selection, shim provenance, Android boot image geometry, partition
writes, and flashing are outside this tool's scope.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.B --ramdisk
Build an ABLXRD1 external-initrd container instead of appending a package to a
shim.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I KERNEL
A raw arm64 Image, Image.gz, Image.zst, or Linux EFI zboot image.
.TP
.I SHIM
A raw abl-exorcist arm64 Image built for the target device.
.TP
.I INITRD
The initramfs bytes to place after the compressed kernel.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command exits with status 0 on success and a nonzero status if an input is
invalid or cannot be read, assembly fails, or standard output cannot be
written.
.SH EXAMPLES
Append a kernel package to a shim:
.PP
.EX
abl-exorcist-assembler vmlinuz abl-exorcist.bin > prepared-kernel
.EE
.PP
Build the external-initrd transport used as an Android ramdisk:
.PP
.EX
abl-exorcist-assembler --ramdisk vmlinuz initramfs.img > ablx-ramdisk.img
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dracut (8),
.BR gzip (1),
.BR zstd (1)
